{"entryId":"3207","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3207:1","sourceSha256":"1312fcbef6eb95eabd8b59e0395bc9579fa7a3b62492a001667cf6457d938c81","englishSha256":"c56f8b394a695f021c87f86bb37522dfa3f0f21012807377c43d16f4e47ed055","citations":[{"id":"3207:1:link-001","he":[5,27],"en":[7,45],"target":{"entry":164,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 164:1","assessment":"The named Avin catalogue contains the precise Pesahim parallel and calls the Adda form a correction. The broader heading points to the whole name cluster.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 164:1","target":{"entry":164,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3207:1:link-002","he":[45,71],"en":[67,91],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_42a.3"},"reference":"Yoma 42a:3","assessment":"Yoma gives Ravya bar Kisi in the report of death and repeats the name in the mnemonic.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 42a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_42a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3207:1:link-003","he":[73,100],"en":[93,119],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_20b.4"},"reference":"Chullin 20b:4","assessment":"The checked Chullin reads Ravin bar Kisi rather than Kisa. Preserve the gloss’s consonantal alternative.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 20b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_20b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3207:1:link-004","he":[102,128],"en":[121,152],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_63a.3"},"reference":"Bava Batra 63a:3","assessment":"The third form is directly attested.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 63a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_63a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3207:1:link-005","he":[152,210],"en":[260,387],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_34a.1"},"reference":"Pesachim 34a:1","assessment":"The received text gives R. Avin bar Rav Aha in the name of R. Yitzhak. The Avin dossier gives the same proposal to read Adda. The emendation is not silently substituted.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 34a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_34a.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 164:1","target":{"entry":164,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3207:1:link-006","he":[215,243],"en":[392,420],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_75b.14"},"reference":"Chullin 75b:14","assessment":"The checked source explicitly gives Ravin bar Hanina reporting Ulla in Rabbi Hanina’s name.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 75b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_75b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"holds":[{"raw":"ל\"ת, צ\"ע איזה יכשר","reason":"The three received passages preserve different names. The gloss itself does not decide. The abbreviation remains provisional for this glossing series.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 42a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_42a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 20b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_20b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 63a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_63a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"וברוב מקומות חיננא ל\"ת","reason":"The named folio reads Hanina. The gloss’s generalization about other occurrences, and the precise interpretation of the siglum, remain qualified.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 75b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_75b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The exact Avin catalogue reports the Adda emendation. Yoma, Hullin and Bava Batra preserve